course: dictionary
lesson: 15253
title: Shona: a people, a language, a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Shona is one of them. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning is right. Look at the words around it, and ask: is this a person, a thing, or a name?
explain: «The Shona people live mainly in Zimbabwe.» Here Shona means a group of people. «Mia can speak Shona with her grandmother.» Here Shona means a language. «Shona waved at me from the far side of the playground.» Here Shona is a girl's name.
explain: Sometimes Shona works like a describing word. «The museum had a beautiful Shona sculpture carved from stone.» The word Shona tells you what kind of sculpture it is. Capital letters are a clue too: Shona starts with a capital when it names a people, a language or a person.
fact: Shona is a people of southern Africa, and most of them live in Zimbabwe.
fact: Shona is also a language, and it is one of the official languages of Zimbabwe.
fact: Shona is a girl's first name, mostly found in Scotland and Ireland.
fact: «Shona sculpture» means carvings in stone made in the Shona style, and it is famous around the world.
fact: Great Zimbabwe, an ancient stone city, is linked with the ancestors of the Shona people.
exercise: «The Shona people live in southern Africa.» What does Shona mean here? | A kind of stone | *A people | A petrol station | A river in Scotland
exercise: «Mia can speak Shona, so she talks with her grandmother in it.» What does Shona mean here? | A kind of drum | *A language | A city | A girl's name
exercise: «The gallery sold a beautiful Shona sculpture carved from stone.» What is Shona describing? | The colour of the paint | The size of the room | *The style of the carving | The price of the gallery
test: «Shona laughed and waved at us from across the playground.» What does Shona mean here? | *A girl's first name | A language spoken in Scotland | A kind of stone | A people of Zimbabwe
test: Which country are the Shona people mainly found in? | Kenya | Scotland | *Zimbabwe | Ireland
exam: «Our teacher said Shona is one of the official languages of Zimbabwe.» What does Shona mean here? | A river | A kind of food | A boy's name | *A language
